    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.comment\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.12 (!at least latest Nightly build!)\n\n### Description\n\nI just updated to the stable release of 0.12 and immediately noticed that mini.comment is currently broken. I have been using the 0.12 nightly from time to time and can't recall having that problem there, but maybe I just didn't try to use the commenting function.\n\nI'd love if this would get fixed soon as I constantly use it :) As well as many other mini.nvim plugins of course, hehe :) \n\nThank you for the amazing collection of plugins and all the best\n\nJanis\n\n### Reproduction\n\nSimply open any file, then try to comment out one or more lines with gcc and you will get a lua error:\nE5108: Lua: ...ext-commentstring/lua/ts_context_commentstring/utils.lua:103: attempt to index local 'language_tree' (a nil value)\nstack traceback:\n\t...ext-commentstring/lua/ts_context_commentstring/utils.lua:103: in function 'get_node_at_cursor_start_of_line'\n\t...-commentstring/lua/ts_context_commentstring/internal.lua:56: in function 'calculate_commentstring'\n\t...zyVim/lua/lazyvim/plugins/extras/coding/mini-comment.lua:8: in function 'custom_commentstring'\n\t....local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.comment/lua/mini/comment.lua:460: in function 'get_comment_parts'\n\t....local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.comment/lua/mini/comment.lua:245: in function 'toggle_lines'\n\t....local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.comment/lua/mini/comment.lua:203: in function <....local/share/nvim/lazy/mini.comment/lua/mini/comment.lua:173>",
