        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I am not sure what you mean with the custom commentstring, I've never set up anything like that. I'm also using LazyVim and mini.comment as part of LazyExtras, so maybe it's something about Lazy's config.\n\nYes, `ts_context_commentstring` is configured as part of the ['mini.comment' LazyExtra](https://www.lazyvim.org/extras/coding/mini-comment).\n\n> Maybe you have any other ideas what could cause the issue here?\n\nBased only on the traceback from the first comment, I am fairly certain that the issue comes not from 'mini.comment' but from ['JoosepAlviste/nvim-ts-context-commentstring'](https://github.com/JoosepAlviste/nvim-ts-context-commentstring) plugin. The best course of action here is to report an issue to that plugin. Although it seems there are already PRs to fix this (JoosepAlviste/nvim-ts-context-commentstring#124 and/or JoosepAlviste/nvim-ts-context-commentstring#125), they are just not merged yet.",
